values.value:
Generate a code-output question that shows a snippet of Apex (or SOQL/LWC JavaScript) code and asks what it produces or what error it throws. Return a single valid JSON object with the following fields: - "questionText": string, asking what the output or result of the provided code snippet is - "code": string, the code snippet to display (use 
 for line breaks, indent with spaces not tabs) - "options": array of 4 objects each with "id" (A/B/C/D) and "text" (the answer choice representing an output, error, or result) - "correctAnswer": string, the single option id that is the correct output/result - "explanation": string, 2-3 sentences explaining what the code does step by step and why the correct output is produced
Example output: { "questionText": "What is the output of the following Apex code?", "code": "Integer x = 5;
Integer y = 10;
System.debug(x + y + ' items');
System.debug('' + x + y + ' items');", "options": [ {"id": "A", "text": "15 items and 510 items"}, {"id": "B", "text": "15 items and 15 items"}, {"id": "C", "text": "510 items and 510 items"}, {"id": "D", "text": "A runtime exception is thrown"} ], "correctAnswer": "A", "explanation": "In the first debug, x+y evaluates as integer addition (15) before string concatenation. In the second debug, the empty string forces left-to-right string concatenation, making x concatenate to '5' then y appends '10', producing '510 items'." }
